.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std ark
.Pp
The
.Nm
utility uses the following non-zero exit statuses:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 1
Usage error.
.It 2
Input/output or filesystem error.
.It 3
Archive format error.
.It 4
Integrity error.
.It 5
Security error.
.It 6
Source consistency error.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create an archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark create archive.ark path
.Ed
.Pp
Create an archive using SHA-256:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark create --hash sha256 archive.ark path
.Ed
.Pp
List archive members:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark list archive.ark
.Ed
.Pp
Extract into a directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark extract --output restored archive.ark
.Ed
.Pp
Extract a single member:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark extract --member path/in/archive archive.ark
.Ed
.Pp
Verify an archive:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark verify archive.ark
.Ed
.Pp
Generate and compile a recovery reader:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ark generate-reader recovery.c
$ cc -O2 recovery.c -o recover
.Ed
.Sh KNOWN LIMITATIONS
The following are design limitations, not defects:
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fl -overwrite
is not rollback-safe.
If extraction fails after replacing an existing file, the original file
contents are lost.
.It
The recovery reader covers the v1 format only.
.It
The entire index is loaded and verified in memory.
.It
The writer buffers index metadata in memory until all member data is written.
.It
Compression is always enabled.
There is no store-only mode.
.It
ACLs, SELinux contexts, and extended attributes are not preserved.
.It
Member paths are limited to 1023 bytes.
.It
Concurrent writes to the same target path are not coordinated.
.It
Only local POSIX filesystem behaviour is in scope.
.It
Numeric uid and gid values are not portable across systems.
.It
Existing archives cannot be appended to or updated in place.
.It
A crash may leave an orphaned libchevron temporary file in the target parent
directory.
.It
The v1 chunk size is fixed at 1MB.
.It
Deflate optimisations must preserve v1 format invariants.
.It
Source modification detection is limited to mtime and size changes while each
file is being read.
.It
On Linux 5.13 through 5.18, archives containing hardlinks are rejected before
filesystem side effects because hardlink extraction requires Landlock ABI v2.
.It
Cleanup failure after an extraction error may leave residual extracted content.
.It
.Cm generate-reader
writes a separate companion C source file that must be kept with long-term
archives.
.It
Hardlink extraction on Linux requires Linux 5.19 or newer.
.El
